{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 25, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "John woke up to the sound of birds chirping and a gentle breeze rustling the leaves of the digital trees surrounding him. He rubbed his eyes in confusion, realizing that the world around him was too vivid, too perfect—almost as if it were rendered by a computer. His hands, his surroundings, even the air he breathed, all felt hyper-real yet undeniably artificial. Panic set in as he tried to recall his last memory: a late-night gaming session, his avatar left mid-quest in a fantasy realm. Now, here he was, standing in the same realm, but as the avatar itself. His heart pounded as he noticed a health bar flicker at the corner of his vision, confirming his worst fear—he was no longer a player, but a character in the game.\n\n***\n\nHe sprinted through the pixelated village, dodging NPCs who went about their routines oblivious to his plight. A quest prompt popped up in his vision: *\"Find the Ancient Amulet to unlock the next level.\"* He scoffed—this was supposed to be a simple fetch quest, not a matter of life or death. Desperate, he ducked into an alley and tried to interact with his inventory, only to find it glitching, items flickering in and out of existence. A glint of hope appeared when he spotted a save point—a glowing shrine—but as he reached for it, the screen flickered violently. His vision blurred, and for a terrifying moment, he saw his own bedroom through the distortion before the world snapped back into place. The game was fighting him, refusing to let him escape.", "logprobs": [{"token": "John", "logprob": -1.7567740678787231}, {"token": " woke", "logprob": -1.443169116973877}, {"token": " up", "logprob": -0.13699430227279663}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.16900023818016052}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.04795655608177185}, {"token": " sound", "logprob": -0.14726349711418152}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -1.311301275563892e-0